DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI VehicleCostPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
plus the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant over an injectable VehicleCostDataSource seam whose value
types mirror the KMP OperatorConfidence VehicleCostResponse 1:1 (production binds
OperatorConfidenceStore.vehicleCost() through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the four fleet StatCards (Total rows /
Total bytes / Rate / DLQ failures, each with its web sublabel, shown whenever the server totals are
present — including the zero-vehicle success), and the per-vehicle breakdown GlassPanel with the
window Select and an adaptive table — a columnar Grid on macOS/iPad and per-vehicle cards on iPhone —
covering all six web columns (with the DLQ amber emphasis + display_name fallback), using the P2
tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass). Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (28 keys added; admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle reused);
display formatting (fmtNumber/formatBytes/formatRelative) is ported and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH
idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0 macOS+iOS) and an executed model harness
(46/46); my four source files are confirmed compiled in the full app target's SwiftFileList with ZERO
diagnostics. The full-scheme xcodebuild is RED ONLY due to pre-existing, out-of-scope sibling files
(shared-surfaces / DriveScore), which are forbidden to commit-fix — exactly the DiskForecast precedent.

